                                          2168  #-----------------------------------------------------------------------
                                          2169  #
                                          2170  #  vCPU extension functions (for acceleration and compaction) follow below.
                                          2171  #
                                          2172  #  The naming convention is: SYS_<CamelCase>[_v<V>]_<N>
                                          2173  #
                                          2174  #  With <N> the maximum number of cycles the function will run
                                          2175  #  (counted from NEXT to NEXT). This is the same number that must
                                          2176  #  be passed to the 'SYS' vCPU instruction as operand, and it will
                                          2177  #  appear in the GCL code upon use.
                                          2178  #
                                          2179  #  If a SYS extension got introduced after ROM v1, the version number of
                                          2180  #  introduction is included in the name. This helps the programmer to be
                                          2181  #  reminded to verify the acutal ROM version and fail gracefully on older
                                          2182  #  ROMs than required. See also Docs/GT1-files.txt on using [romType].
                                          2183  #
                                          2184  #-----------------------------------------------------------------------
                                          2185
